From: CharlyRien <9572419+CharlyRien@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:30:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] Lab: XCL_TEX_KEY_PAD=1 keys view-by-address textures
 without the padding at 4..8, counted either way

After xcl-dev/xcl#3000 by voiceovarian1-max: resource_at's key also leaves
out bytes 4..8 of the resource desc (the padding after the dimension, before
the 8-byte aligned width), which hold whatever the title's stack held there.
Here behind a lab switch, OFF by default: without it the textures made and
the desc given to the device are as before.

The table is now keyed by address and desc without that padding, each key
keeping the paddings it was asked with and the texture made for each, so the
pad-only duplicates are counted with no second table and no other lock:
- switch off: a padding not seen for a key makes the texture again (counted
  as a pad-only duplicate made);
- switch on: the texture already made is served (counted as served).
"lab tex key:" line every 10 s on the activity thread, whatever the switch:
textures made, refused, pad-only duplicates made, served (atomics only).

Unit tests without the GPU: the key zeroes 4..8 and 0x34.. only and keeps
0..4 and 8..0x34; the counts with the switch off and on; a texture made twice
at once is no duplicate. No file of TRANSLATOR_SOURCES touched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
